WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.728
The PM skills that transfer.

2
00:00:02.008 --> 00:00:13.592
If you’ve led product or projects, you already have most of what directing agents needs; it just has to be applied more literally, because an agent won’t ask the hallway question a colleague would.

3
00:00:13.872 --> 00:00:16.304
Scoping: say what’s in and out, in writing.

4
00:00:16.584 --> 00:00:20.083
Acceptance criteria: make done observable and testable.

5
00:00:20.363 --> 00:00:25.632
Dependency planning: sequence work that shares interfaces, parallelize what doesn’t.

6
00:00:25.912 --> 00:00:29.560
Work breakdown: deliverables small enough to review in one sitting.

7
00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:36.027
Status with evidence: a step is done when a check passed and the commit exists, not when someone says it’s done.

8
00:00:36.307 --> 00:00:41.128
Risk management: identify the irreversible steps and keep them for a person.

9
00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:52.288
The difference from managing people is that agents are tireless, fast, literal, and confidently wrong at times, so the documents you write and the checks you require carry more of the load.
